---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

/** Shown under the heading. Change it whenever the terms change. */
const lastUpdated = '5 November 2026';
---

<Layout title="terms" description="The terms for using Cueory." noindex>
  <Prose>
    <h1>terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is a free study site for nursing students. Use it to study. Don't copy it, break it or use it to harm
      anyone. It is a study aid, not medical advice, and we can't promise it is error-free. If you don't agree with these
      terms, please don't use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Who these terms are between</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are an agreement between you and {site.name} ("we", "us"). They cover the website at
      <a href={site.url}>{site.url}</a> and everything on it: lessons, cards, questions, the anatomy lab, daily games and
      accounts. By using the site you accept them. If we change them, we update the date above; if a change matters, we
      say so on the site before it takes effect.
    </p>

    <h2>Who may use the site</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 16 years old to use {site.name}. You may use it for your own study. If you are a teacher or a
      program, you may point your students to it; please don't copy it into your own materials without asking us first.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      An account is optional. If you create one, keep your sign-in to yourself and tell us if you think someone else has
      used it. You are responsible for what happens under your account. You may delete it at any time from the
      <a href="/account">account page</a>; deleting it removes your account and the study data linked to it, as the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> explains.
    </p>

    <h2>Our content</h2>
    <p>
      The lessons, questions, cards, puzzles, artwork and the {site.name} name and logo belong to us or to the people who
      let us use them. You may read, study and share links to our pages. You may not copy, scrape, resell or republish
      our content, build another product on it, or remove notices from it, without our written permission. Some
      material is used under its own license, named where it appears, and keeps that license.
    </p>

    <h2>What you send us</h2>
    <p>
      When you send a report with the "Flag or comment" button or write to us, you give us permission to use what you
      send to fix and improve the site. Don't send anything you don't have the right to share, or anything about a
      real patient.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair use of the site</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>try to get around sign-in, rate limits, answer checking or any other protection;</li>
      <li>use scripts or bots to pull answers, questions or other content in bulk;</li>
      <li>probe, overload or interfere with the site or the services behind it;</li>
      <li>upload harmful code, or use the site to harass, impersonate or deceive anyone;</li>
      <li>use the site in a way that breaks the law.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you find a security problem, please tell us at
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> rather than using it.
    </p>

    <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} helps you study. It is not medical, nursing or clinical advice, and it is not a substitute for your
      program, your instructors, your textbooks or a licensed clinician. Never make a decision about a real patient
      based on something you read here. Our <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a> says more.
    </p>

    <h2>No promises about accuracy or availability</h2>
    <p>
      We work hard to keep the content right and the site up, but we provide {site.name} "as is", without warranties of
      any kind. Content may be incomplete, out of date or wrong; exam blueprints and clinical guidance change. Features
      may change or stop, and the site may be unavailable sometimes. Study with more than one source.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits on our liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent the law allows, {site.name} and the people who run it are not liable for any indirect,
      incidental or consequential loss, or for any loss arising from your use of the site or your reliance on its
      content, including exam results and clinical outcomes. Where the law does not allow this limit, our liability is
      limited to the smallest amount it permits. Nothing here limits rights the law gives you that cannot be waived.
    </p>

    <h2>Support and tips</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is free. If you choose to support it with a tip, that is a gift, not a purchase: it buys no features,
      services or promises, and it isn't refundable except where the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending</h2>
    <p>
      You may stop using the site at any time and delete your account. We may suspend or close an account that breaks
      these terms, and we may stop offering the site or any part of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Which law applies</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Arizona, United States, without regard to conflict-of-law
      rules. If a part of these terms turns out to be unenforceable, the rest still applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
